<article class="env-lemma" id="0F5G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F5G">Lemma <span data-tag="0F5G">115.8.28</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes which is locally quasi-finite. For an abelian group $A$ and a geometric point $\overline{y} : \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \to Y$ we have $f^!(\overline{y}_*A) = \prod \nolimits _{f(\overline{x}) = \overline{y}} \overline{x}_*A$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from the corresponding statement in More Étale Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0F59" data-tag="0F59">63.6.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>